course: dictionary
lesson: 438
title: A link between animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Archaeopteryx is the name of one animal that lived a very long time ago. You can work out what it is from the words around it. «Archaeopteryx, about 150 million years old, had feathered wings but also teeth, claws and a long bony tail.» Feathers and wings sound like a bird, but teeth and a bony tail sound like a dinosaur.
explain: Scientists call an animal like this an in-between animal, because it links two groups. The clues are in the sentence: it has parts of both. «Archaeopteryx ... just the in-between kind Darwin's idea expected.» Here the words in-between kind tell you it sits halfway between dinosaurs and birds.
explain: The name also has a clue. It comes from Greek and means ancient wing. Ancient means very old, and wing is the part that helps an animal fly. So even before you read the rest, the name tells you it is an old animal with wings.
fact: Archaeopteryx means ancient wing in Greek.
fact: It lived about 150 million years ago, in what is now Germany.
fact: It had feathers and wings like a bird, but teeth, claws and a long bony tail like a dinosaur.
fact: It was about the size of a crow or magpie.
fact: Scientists still discuss how well it could fly.
fact: Its fossils were found in limestone, and one was found in 1861.
exercise: «Archaeopteryx had feathered wings but also teeth, claws and a long bony tail.» Which two groups of animals does it mix? | Cats and dogs | Insects and frogs | *Birds and dinosaurs | Fish and whales
exercise: Archaeopteryx is Greek for ancient wing. What does ancient mean? | Very new | *Very old | Very small | Very fast
exercise: «Archaeopteryx ... was found in Germany in 1861.» Where was it found? | Greece | Australia | *Germany | Scotland
test: Archaeopteryx was about the size of what? | A cat | *A crow or magpie | An elephant | A horse
test: Why do scientists call Archaeopteryx an in-between animal? | It was half fish and half frog | It lived in the sea | *It had features of both dinosaurs and birds | It was a plant
exam: Which sentence best describes Archaeopteryx? | A modern bird that lives in gardens today | A whale found in Germany | *A small animal from long ago with features of dinosaurs and birds | A kind of tree found in Scotland
